course: dictionary
lesson: 8624
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The word scroll is a good example. You can scroll on a screen, you can read an old scroll made of rolled-up paper, and a scroll can be a curly decoration. Context tells you which meaning the writer means.
explain: «Jake scrolls up and sees himself called Professor Sam.» Jake is looking at a screen, so scroll means move the text up to see more. «The Torah is handwritten on scrolls» is about long rolls of paper or parchment, not a screen.
explain: Always check the clues. What is being moved or read? Is it a screen, a rolled paper, or a curl in a design? Then put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: To scroll means to move the text or pictures on a screen up, down or sideways to see more.
fact: A scroll is a long roll of paper or parchment with writing on it, used in ancient times.
fact: A scroll can also be a decoration shaped like a curl.
fact: Endless scrolling on apps can waste a lot of time, so it is wise to set limits.
fact: Scroll is both a verb and a noun, so the context tells you which one it is.
exercise: «Jake scrolls up and sees himself called Professor Sam.» What does scrolls mean here? | To roll up a long piece of paper | To draw a curl on a decoration | *To move the text on a screen up to see more | To write in ink on parchment
exercise: «The ancient Egyptians wrote on papyrus scrolls.» What is a scroll in this sentence? | A phone app that keeps you looking | *A long roll of paper with writing on it | Some curly decorations on a door | A bar at the side of a web page
exercise: «The carved wooden door had a scroll at each corner.» What does scroll mean here? | *A decoration shaped like a curl | A sad or tired feeling | A long roll of paper | To move the text on a screen
test: «Mia could not stop scrolling through videos until midnight.» What does scrolling mean? | Rolling up old paper | Reading a book quietly | Curling a decoration | *Moving through a screen to see more
test: «The wizard unrolled a magic scroll with glowing writing.» What is the scroll? | *A long roll of paper or parchment with writing on it | A bar at the side of a screen | A curly decoration on a wall | To move the text up and down
exam: «The Torah is read from a scroll in the synagogue.» Which meaning of scroll fits best, and why? | A bar on a web page, because it is long | *A long roll of parchment with writing on it, because it is read like a rolled-up book | To move the text on a screen, because people read on screens in synagogues | A decoration shaped like a curl, because you read it on a wall
